        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>The effectiveness of intrauterine contraceptive devices exceeds that of most family planning methods and approaches that of oral contraceptives in continuing users. There has been some evidence of endometrial reaction in patients fitted with intrauterine devices and some postinsertion disturbances have been observed. The IUD is free of major complications provided indications for use are carefully defined and patient management is adequate.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
